\par\par \uc2 National Desk; SECTA\par \b \uc2 Harris Is Expected to Call for National Legislation to Protect  \highlight22\uc2 Reproductive Rights \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 By Katie Rogers \par \uc2 601 \uc2 words\par \uc2 19 January 2023\par \uc2 The New York Times\par \uc2 NYTF\par \uc2 Late Edition - Final\par 16\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2023 The New York Times Company.  All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 She will contrast the Biden administration's efforts with Republicans across the country who have tried to curtail access to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and some forms of contraception since the ruling was overturned.\par \par \uc2 WASHINGTON -- \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 , the vice president, will travel to Florida on Sunday to deliver a speech commemorating the 50th anniversary of Roe v. Wade, the landmark Supreme Court ruling that established a constitutional right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  but was overturned last summer.\par \par \uc2 She will also criticize Republicans across the country who have tried to curtail access to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and some forms of contraception in the months since the ruling was overturned, according to officials within her office who outlined the speech on the condition of anonymity.\par \par \uc2 As the post-Roe landscape in America takes shape, with a patchwork of states working to restrict \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access or ban it outright, the White House has few options beyond using the bully pulpit to spur support for \b \highlight22\uc2 reproductive rights\b0 \highlight\uc2  from state to state.\par \par \uc2 Without the votes in the Senate to enshrine the protections offered by Roe into law, and with the president unable to grant those protections through executive action, administration officials hope Ms. Harris's appearance in Florida will help sustain the sort of anger that became a driving force for voters during the midterm elections.\par \par \uc2 ''The vice president will make very clear: The fight to secure women's fundamental right to \b \highlight22\uc2 reproductive health\b0 \highlight\uc2  care is far from over,'' her press secretary, Kirsten Allen, said in a statement. ''She will lay out the consequences of extremist attacks on reproductive freedom in states across our country and underscore the need for Congress to codify Roe.'' She added that the president and the vice president are clear that a woman's right to choose is ''nonnegotiable.''\par \par \uc2 Her office would not say on Wednesday where in the state she will visit. The event also presents Ms. Harris with another opportunity to establish herself as the administration's leading voice on promoting \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights, a position she has embraced in recent months. According to her office, Ms. Harris has hosted leaders from 38 states in events known as ''convenings,'' and has gathered dozens of state legislators from 18 states to discuss \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access.\par \par \uc2 In her speech on Sunday, she is expected to call for national legislation to protect \b \highlight22\uc2 reproductive rights\b0 \highlight\uc2 , even though President Biden has said repeatedly that the Senate lacks the votes to do so. She is also expected to highlight the executive action Mr. Biden signed last summer, with provisions that include defending patients' right to travel across state lines to receive medical care and issuing guidance to retail pharmacies.\par \par \uc2 Ms. Harris's trip to Florida, the country's third most-populous state, is not a coincidence: Abortions after 15 weeks of pregnancy are banned there. Republicans, fresh from winning supermajorities in the Florida legislature, have discussed changing the timeline to 12 weeks. Earlier this month, after the \uc2 Food and Drug Administration\uc2  issued a regulation allowing the sale of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pills at retail pharmacies, Florida health officials warned pharmacists not to dispense the pills.\par \par \uc2 While Ms. Harris speaks in Florida on Sunday, Mr. Biden will issue a proclamation commemorating Roe, one of dozens he makes to mark events each year. Other administration officials are making trips to highlight the importance of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access. On Thursday, \uc2 Xavier Becerra\uc2 , the secretary of Health and Human Services, will travel to Minnesota, where officials are working to expand access to \b \highlight22\uc2 reproductive health\b0 \highlight\uc2  care.\par \par \uc2 This article appeared in print on page A16. \par \par \uc2 Document NYTF000020230119ej1j0003r\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw284\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal4260\pichgoal600
