\par\par \uc2 National Desk; SECTA\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Abortion \highlight\uc2  Ban Is Reinstated In Georgia\b0\par\par\uc2 By Ava Sasani \par \uc2 470 \uc2 words\par \uc2 24 November 2022\par \uc2 The New York Times\par \uc2 NYTF\par \uc2 Late Edition - Final\par 14\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 The New York Times Company.  All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 The order comes after a lower court ruled last week that the ban was unconstitutional.\par \par \uc2 The Georgia Supreme Court on Wednesday reinstated the state's ban on abortions after six weeks of pregnancy, temporarily restoring the law that had been blocked by a lower court last week.\par \par \uc2 The State Supreme Court's order, in response to a request for an emergency stay by the \uc2 Georgia attorney general's office\uc2 , comes one week after Judge Robert C.I. McBurney of Fulton County Superior Court suspended the law. He said he had done so because the six-week ban was unconstitutional when the state legislature approved it in 2019 -- more than three years before the \uc2 U.S. Supreme Court\uc2  revoked the constitutional right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The ban after six weeks of pregnancy -- a time when most women have not yet realized they are pregnant -- is not a final decision but will remain in effect while the State Supreme Court considers the attorney general's appeal of Judge McBurney's ruling.\par \par \uc2 ''We are pleased with the court's action today. However, we are unable to provide further comment due to the pending appeal,'' said Kara Richardson, a spokesman for the attorney general's office.\par \par \uc2 The State Supreme Court also denied a request by \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  providers and \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -rights advocates for a 24-hour notice before reinstating the ban.\par \par \uc2 According to a statement from \uc2 the American Civil Liberties Union\uc2 , one of the organizations that had filed a lawsuit against the ban, patients who had scheduled \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  appointments were being turned away on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 A spokeswoman for Planned Parenthood, Olivia Cappello, said all providers in the state immediately halted \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  services for patients who have detectable fetal heartbeat activity.\par \par \uc2 ''Our state's \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  providers are again being forced to turn away patients who then must leave the state for safe, time-sensitive and essential health care,'' said Amy Kennedy, vice president for external affairs of Planned Parenthood Southeast.\par \par \uc2 The issue of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been front and center in Georgia, where a tight \uc2 U.S. Senate\uc2  race between a Democratic incumbent, Raphael Warnock, and a Republican challenger, \uc2 Herschel Walker\uc2 , is headed to a runoff on Dec. 6.\par \par \uc2 Two women have said that Mr. Walker urged them to have abortions, and, in one case, one said that Mr. Walker paid for the procedure. Mr. Walker, who denied the claims, said he supported the state's \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban.\par \par \uc2 Mr. Warnock said he supports \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights as outlined in Roe v. Wade, which said that a woman had the constitutional right to end her pregnancy until the fetus could survive outside the womb, which is usually around 23 weeks. The \uc2 U.S. Supreme Court\uc2  eliminated that right in June.\par \par \uc2 This article appeared in print on page A14. \par \par \uc2 Document NYTF000020221124eibo0003q\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw284\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal4260\pichgoal600
