\par\par \uc2 National Desk; SECTA\par \b \uc2 New Unnamed Walker Accuser Emerges\b0\par\par\uc2 By Jonathan Weisman and Maya King \par \uc2 839 \uc2 words\par \uc2 27 October 2022\par \uc2 The New York Times\par \uc2 NYTF\par \uc2 Late Edition - Final\par 18\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 The New York Times Company.  All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 The woman delivered her story anonymously in a news conference with Gloria Allred, the celebrity lawyer. \uc2 The New York Times\uc2  could not confirm the account.\par \par \uc2 A woman who did not identify herself said on Wednesday that \uc2 Herschel Walker\uc2  pressured her to have an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and paid for the procedure nearly three decades ago after a yearslong extramarital relationship. A former football star, Mr. Walker is running for the Senate in Georgia as an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  opponent.\par \par \uc2 The New York Times\uc2  could not confirm the account, interview the woman or inspect the evidence that Gloria Allred, the celebrity lawyer, asserted was proof that the woman had a relationship with Mr. Walker.\par \par \uc2 The woman told her story at a news conference with Ms. Allred, but did not appear on camera. Neither she nor Ms. Allred offered any evidence to back up the woman's accusation that Mr. Walker, a Republican, had urged her to end her pregnancy even after she initially left an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinic without going through with the procedure.\par \par \uc2 The evidence provided included a taped message from a man Ms. Allred said was Mr. Walker calling from the Winter Olympics of 1992, where Mr. Walker competed in bobsled; a number of greeting cards signed ''H''; and a blurry photo of a man who Ms. Allred said was Mr. Walker in a hotel room in Mankato, Minn. She also showed what she said was a receipt for that hotel, a \uc2 Holiday Inn\uc2  in the city where the \uc2 Minnesota Vikings\uc2 , Mr. Walker's professional football team at the time, practiced.\par \par \uc2 The woman, speaking remotely into the news conference, said she was so traumatized in 1993 after she had the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  that she left her home in the Dallas area and did not return for 15 years.\par \par \uc2 The woman said she was a registered independent who voted for Donald J. Trump, a Republican, in 2016 and 2020. She told her story, she said, to expose hypocrisy in Mr. Walker's campaign message and because, she said, he lied in denying another woman's account of his urging her to have an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  by saying that he never signed cards with just his first initial, ''H.''\par \par \uc2 Shortly before the news conference, Mr. Walker broadly denied the claim at a campaign event in Dillard, Ga., about 100 miles north of Atlanta.\par \par \uc2 ''I'm done with this foolishness. I've already told people this is a lie and I'm not going to entertain it,'' he said, suggesting that this was a reflection of Democratic jitters following his performance during the Senate debate against the Democratic incumbent, Senator Raphael Warnock, this month. ''The Democrats will do and say whatever they can to win this seat.''\par \par \uc2 Just weeks ago, another woman said Mr. Walker had paid for her to have an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in 2009 and urged her to terminate a second pregnancy two years later. They ended their relationship after she refused, that woman, who also refused to be identified, told The Times in a series of interviews.\par \par \uc2 Mr. Walker, who denied that account, has anchored his campaign on an appeal to social conservatives as an unwavering opponent of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  even in cases of rape and incest. He has since wavered on his policy approach to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , saying in September that he would support a measure from Senator \uc2 Lindsey Graham\uc2  of South Carolina that would ban \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  nationwide after 15 weeks of pregnancy and declaring his support during the Senate debate for Georgia's new law that outlaws the procedure after six weeks.\par \par \uc2 A spokesman for Mr. Walker did not immediately respond to a request for comment on the specifics of the new claim.\par \par \uc2 Mr. Warnock's campaign released a statement calling the new accusation ''just the latest example of a troubling pattern we have seen play out again and again and again,'' saying Mr. Walker has ''a problem with the truth.''\par \par \uc2 Mr. Walker has been dogged by a series of potentially damaging reports about his personal life since he began his campaign for Senate in 2021. In June, The Daily Beast reported that Mr. Walker, who has criticized absentee fathers in Black households, had fathered a child out of wedlock. Later that week, the outlet reported on two more children he had not previously mentioned publicly or to his campaign aides.\par \par \uc2 Mr. Walker acknowledged an extramarital affair in his 2009 memoir, ''Breaking Free: My Life With Dissociative Identity Disorder.'' He described a relationship with a woman who lived in Irving, Tex., a Dallas suburb.\par \par \uc2 ''I just want to convey that I knew right from wrong and I did a very, very wrong thing that hurt my wife, another person and in the end me,'' he wrote.\par \par \uc2 Herschel Walker at a campaign event in Cordele, Ga., last week. Another woman has come forth saying he pressured her to get an \uc2  and paid for the procedure. (PHOTOGRAPH BY NICOLE CRAINE FOR THE NEW YORK TIMES) This article appeared in print on page A18. \par \par \uc2 Document NYTF000020221027eiar0004k\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw284\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal4260\pichgoal600
