\par\par \uc2 National Desk; SECTA\par \b \uc2 Defense Secretary Seeks to Reassure Service Members on Access to  \highlight22\uc2 Abortion \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 By Helene Cooper \par \uc2 537 \uc2 words\par \uc2 21 October 2022\par \uc2 The New York Times\par \uc2 NYTF\par \uc2 Late Edition - Final\par 16\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 The New York Times Company.  All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 The Pentagon will provide travel funds and other support for women who seek abortions, a new directive says.\par \par \uc2 WASHINGTON -- Defense Secretary \uc2 Lloyd J. Austin III\uc2  issued a directive on Thursday meant to reassure military service members that the Supreme Court ruling overturning Roe v. Wade would not leave troops without access to abortions in states where the procedure had been banned.\par \par \uc2 The Pentagon will provide travel funds and other support for women who seek abortions but who are based in states where the procedure is illegal, the directive says.\par \par \uc2 It also essentially tells commanders not to ask too many questions when women request leave for \b \highlight22\uc2 reproductive health\b0 \highlight\uc2  care reasons.\par \par \uc2 Mr. Austin said that Pentagon officials had heard from ''many of our service members and their families about the complexity and the uncertainty that they now face in accessing \b \highlight22\uc2 reproductive health\b0 \highlight\uc2  care, including \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  services.''\par \par \uc2 The new policy instructs Defense Department health care providers not to disclose \b \highlight22\uc2 reproductive health\b0 \highlight\uc2  information to commanders unless such info poses a risk to the mission. And it advises the Pentagon to develop a program to support and reimburse Defense Department health care providers who are fined or targeted by states for providing abortions.\par \par \uc2 Mr. Austin directed the services to implement the changes by the end of the year.\par \par \uc2 But it was far from clear whether the directive would give women in the military who seek to end unwanted pregnancies the protection to do so in medically safe ways.\par \par \uc2 The Supreme Court's June decision to strike down Roe v. Wade, ending the constitutional right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , has become one of the defining issues in the midterm elections, with Democrats promising to seek to expand access to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  if they are returned to control of both houses of Congress with enough votes to pass such a measure.\par \par \uc2 The Hyde Amendment prohibits the use of federal funds for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  except in cases of rape or incest, or when the patient's life is at risk. But after the Supreme Court's ruling, some states have banned the procedure, with no exceptions.\par \par \uc2 Pentagon officials say that when a pregnant service member's life is threatened, the Hyde Amendment's stipulations would supersede any state bans.\par \par \uc2 ''I am committed to the department taking all appropriate action, within its authority and consistent with applicable federal law, as soon as possible to ensure that our service members and their families can access \b \highlight22\uc2 reproductive health\b0 \highlight\uc2  care and our health care providers can operate effectively,'' Mr. Austin said in the memorandum.\par \par \uc2 Pentagon officials acknowledge that there is not much they can do for women in states where abortions are prohibited but say that the directive to commanders is meant to provide some help.\par \par \uc2 Defense officials, who were already worried about meeting recruiting goals, are concerned that the court's ruling will affect the department's ability to recruit and retain service members, who could be assigned to a state that has banned \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The military has a number of major bases in states -- including Texas and Florida -- where anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  laws are now in place.\par \par \uc2 This article appeared in print on page A16. \par \par \uc2 Document NYTF000020221021eial0003a\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw284\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal4260\pichgoal600
